WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.583
There's one map

00:00:00.583 --> 00:00:01.835
you have to see to understand

00:00:01.835 --> 00:00:03.670
this conflict between Hamas and Israel.

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:05.255
Gaza is this small strip of land

00:00:05.255 --> 00:00:06.131
that has 2 million

00:00:06.131 --> 00:00:07.507
Palestinians living in it.

00:00:07.507 --> 00:00:09.467
After a short war in the ‘60s

00:00:09.467 --> 00:00:11.261
Israel captured a bunch of land.

00:00:11.261 --> 00:00:12.762
The map went from looking like this

00:00:12.762 --> 00:00:13.555
to this.

00:00:13.555 --> 00:00:14.222
Israel eventually

00:00:14.222 --> 00:00:15.515
gave Sinai back to Egypt,

00:00:15.515 --> 00:00:16.891
but they continued to occupy

00:00:16.891 --> 00:00:18.727
this small strip of land called Gaza.

00:00:18.727 --> 00:00:19.477
In 2005,

00:00:19.477 --> 00:00:20.895
Israel withdrew from Gaza

00:00:20.895 --> 00:00:22.564
and turned it over to the authority

00:00:22.564 --> 00:00:23.440
of the Palestinians.

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:24.816
It was quickly taken over by this

00:00:24.816 --> 00:00:27.068
anti-Israel group called Hamas,

00:00:27.068 --> 00:00:28.653
which gets us back to this map.

00:00:28.653 --> 00:00:30.280
As soon as Hamas took over Israel

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:30.739
and to lesser

00:00:30.739 --> 00:00:32.198
extent, Egypt started controlling

00:00:32.198 --> 00:00:33.074
everything that went in

00:00:33.074 --> 00:00:33.908
and out of this strip.

00:00:33.908 --> 00:00:35.201
So since Hamas has launched

00:00:35.201 --> 00:00:36.870
these rocket land and sea attacks,

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:38.371
Israel has used this blockade

00:00:38.371 --> 00:00:39.539
to cut off the 2 million

00:00:39.539 --> 00:00:40.665
Palestinians living here

00:00:40.665 --> 00:00:42.625
from fuel, food and supplies.

00:00:42.625 --> 00:00:44.085
Their power plant has run out of gas

00:00:44.085 --> 00:00:45.128
and it is a horrible

00:00:45.128 --> 00:00:46.337
humanitarian situation.

00:00:46.337 --> 00:00:47.797
All of this is yet another chapter

00:00:47.797 --> 00:00:48.757
in this decades long

00:00:48.757 --> 00:00:50.258
pattern of Israeli

00:00:50.258 --> 00:00:52.635
occupation and Palestinian resistance,

00:00:52.635 --> 00:00:53.928
much of it peaceful,

00:00:53.928 --> 00:00:55.388
but some of it like this

00:00:55.388 --> 00:00:56.639
horrifically violent.

